.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WIFI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wifi
.Nd scan for Wi-Fi networks and join, list and forget them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm scan
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm connect
.Op Fl e Cm peap | ttls | ttls-pap
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm forget
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 ,
which
.Xr init 8
runs on
.Ql wlan0 ,
through its control socket
.Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant/wlan0 ,
which only root may use.
wpa_supplicant keeps the known networks in
.Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant/wlan0.conf
and joins the best of them in range by itself, at boot and after the
station loses its network.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm scan
Scan, and list each network in range once, at its strongest access
point, the strongest first: its name, its signal in dBm, its channel, its
protection
.Po
.Ql open ,
.Ql WPA ,
.Ql WPA2 ,
.Ql WPA3 ,
.Ql WPA2/WPA3
or
.Ql enterprise
.Pc ,
and
.Ql known
for a network already known.
A name is shown as wpa_supplicant prints it, a byte that is not
printable as
.Ql \ex Ns Ar NN ,
and
.Cm connect
takes it in the same form.
.It Cm list
List the known networks, with
.Ql in use
for the one the station is joined to,
.Ql disabled
and
.Ql failing
for one wpa_supplicant has stopped trying for a while, and the SHA-256
fingerprint of the server certificate pinned for an enterprise network.
.It Cm connect Ar name
Join
.Ar name .
A known network is selected.
A new one is looked for in the last scan, or in a new scan when it is not
there, and added as its protection asks: an open network as it is, a
personal network with the passphrase
.Nm
asks for, without echo, and an enterprise network with the identity, the
password, an anonymous identity and a server domain it asks for.
A passphrase has 8 to 63 printable characters, or is a key of 64 hex
digits.
.Pp
While it connects, the other known networks are disabled, and they are
enabled again when it ends.
Once the station is joined,
.Nm
has wpa_supplicant save its networks, and prints
.Ql wifi: connected to Ar name .
A new network that cannot be joined, for a wrong passphrase or no answer
in a minute, is not kept.
.Pp
Every network is added with
.Ql bgscan="simple:30:-65:300" :
wpa_supplicant scans every 30 seconds while the signal is below -65 dBm
and every 300 seconds otherwise, moves to a stronger access point of the
same network, and to a stronger known network.
A personal network may be WPA with TKIP, WPA2 or WPA3 with SAE: the
network is added for each, with management frames protected where the
access point offers it, and wpa_supplicant uses the strongest the access
point has.
WEP is not supported.
.It Cm forget Ar name
Remove the known network
.Ar name
and save the networks.
.It Cm status
Print the network the station is joined to, its access point, channel,
signal, protection and address, or that it is not joined, in
wpa_supplicant's state, and why, as the events it logged in
.Pa /var/log/services
since it last joined a network say: a refused passphrase, identity,
password or server certificate.
.El
.Ss Enterprise networks
An enterprise network, WPA2-Enterprise such as eduroam, proves itself to
the station with a server certificate, often one no public authority has
signed.
The first
.Cm connect
pins that certificate, as a phone does: the network is added with
.Ql ca_cert="probe://"
and no password, so that the TLS handshake stops once the server has sent
its certificate, and nothing secret has left the machine.
.Nm
prints the certificate's subject, its name, and its SHA-256 fingerprint,
and asks whether to trust it.
On yes, the network gets
.Ql ca_cert="hash://server/sha256/ Ns Ar fingerprint Ns \&"
and the password, and is joined; on no, it is removed.
Compare the fingerprint with the one the network's administrators publish,
or with the one another device that has joined the network shows.
.Pp
Later connections take no other certificate.
One that does not match is refused, and
.Cm status
prints the certificate presented.
If the administrators changed it,
.Cm forget
and
.Cm connect
the network to trust the new one.
.Pp
The anonymous identity is the outer identity, which goes unencrypted
before the TLS handshake; eduroam asks for
.Ql anonymous@ Ns Ar realm ,
where
.Ar realm
is the part of the identity after its
.Ql @ .
The server domain, when given, is
.Ql domain_suffix_match :
the certificate's name must end in it.
Both may be left empty.
.Pp
The methods are PEAP and TTLS, each with MSCHAPv2 inside, as most
networks use them;
.Fl e
chooses one:
.Bl -tag -width ttls-pap
.It Cm peap
PEAP with MSCHAPv2.
.It Cm ttls
TTLS with MSCHAPv2.
.It Cm ttls-pap
TTLS with PAP, whose password the TLS tunnel carries.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant/wlan0.conf
The known networks, with their passphrases and passwords; only root reads
it.
.It Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant/wlan0
wpa_supplicant's control socket.
.It Pa /var/log/services
The log wpa_supplicant's events go to.
.It Pa /tmp/wifi- Ns Ar pid Ns Pa - Ns Ar n
The two sockets
.Nm
receives wpa_supplicant's replies and events on, removed when it ends.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the command did what it says, 1 when it failed, 2 for a wrong
argument, and 130 when it was interrupted.
A failed or interrupted
.Cm connect
leaves the other networks enabled as they were.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Join a home network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# wifi scan
NAME                              SIGNAL CHANNEL  SECURITY
home                             -41 dBm       6  WPA2/WPA3
# wifi connect home
Passphrase:
wifi: connected to home
.Ed
.Pp
Join a university's network, whose server certificate is self-signed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# wifi connect UNI-WIFI
Identity: student42
Password:
Anonymous identity (empty for none; eduroam's is anonymous@REALM):
Server domain to check (empty for none): radius.uni.edu
UNI-WIFI presents this server certificate:
  subject: /C=KG/O=University/CN=radius.uni.edu
  SHA-256: 5A:1B:C1:29:62:05:E6:FD:BE:39:79:72:8E:FE:39:20
           79:88:85:C1:C4:59:0B:5F:90:F4:32:22:D2:39:CA:6A
Compare the fingerprint with the one the network's administrators publish.
Trust it for this network? [y/N] y
wifi: connected to UNI-WIFI
.Ed
.Pp
Join eduroam with an identity of one's institution:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# wifi connect eduroam
Identity: jdoe@example.edu
Password:
Anonymous identity (empty for none; eduroam's is anonymous@REALM): anonymous@example.edu
Server domain to check (empty for none): example.edu
.Ed
.Pp
and answer the certificate's question as above.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Messages go to standard error as
.Ql wifi: Ar detail ,
such as
.Ql wifi: cannot reach wpa_supplicant at /var/run/wpa_supplicant/wlan0
when wpa_supplicant does not run or the caller is not root, and
.Ql wifi: Ar name : the network refused the passphrase .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr ndwatch 8 ,
.Xr wpa_cli 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 ,
.Xr zzz 8
.Sh BUGS
A hidden network, which does not give its name in its beacons, cannot be
added.
Enterprise networks that want a client certificate (EAP-TLS) are added by
hand in
.Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant/wlan0.conf .
